WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:02.368
 Nick, Josh, congratulations.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.936
You guys are in the
third and final round

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.071
of this competition.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.506
Now, when you came
here, you faced

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:08.674
really tough challenges
that escalated

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.009
throughout the first two rounds.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.878
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:15.548
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history--

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.652
the zhanmadao.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.688 line:14%
JOSH: Holy [bleep].

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:23.523 line:14%
This thing is huge.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.826 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.129
Today, I got to try and figure
out forging on this blade.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.599
I've never made anything
as big as this before.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.067
So it'll be a unique challenge.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:37.370
This is what I'm starting
with, a big old piece 5160.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:39.773
My forge only has
about 18 inches.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.475
And obviously, working on
it a little bit at a time.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:45.811
Try and keep it simple, make
it something drawn out to size.

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:47.847
This thing is going
to be gigantic.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.115
[bleep] damn.

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:51.418
We've got the length.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.585
It's a good start.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.588
End of day one, I got
the whole plate forged

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.123
out to a real rough shape.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.692
Plan for tomorrow is
to get to the quench

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.594 line:14%
by the end of the day.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.630 line:8%
NICK: Yesterday, I was
able to get the blade

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.131
shaped to where I want it.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.902
Now I can get busy
grinding, and hopefully,

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.337
by the end of the day,
to get it quenched.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:15.241
This is going to be a day
filled with attention to detail.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.043
This is the most
nerve wracking part.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.312
This is kind of the
make or break moment.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.584
So get it in the oil, perfect.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.220
I pull it out, [bleep].

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.323
I didn't get a curve on it.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.560
I need it to have a
curve on it, because that

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:38.564
will allow it to function
the way it needs to.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.933
I've got to stick
it back in the fire

00:01:40.999 --> 00:01:42.902
and I've got to get it quenched.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.037
This is not what I
wanted to have happen.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.174
So here we go again,
quench number two.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.844
It didn't break.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.981
Best off, there's a little
bit of a curve in it.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.716
Day two was an adventure.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.185
Pretty happy with where
I'm sitting right now.

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:00.853
So what I'm hoping
to have done tomorrow

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.692
is get the guard fitted up
and be ready for the final day

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.727 line:14%
of fit and finish.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.029 line:8%
JOSH: Morning of day
two, goal for today

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:13.833 line:8%
is to get everything
heat treated.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.703
I'm going about everything
I can to try and get as even

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.771
as possible, but there we go.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:24.610
Coming out of the quench is
going to be a real challenge.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.346
So I clamp it down
with some two-by-fours.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:31.083
The idea here is to help try
and keep it as straight as I can

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.217
while it cools.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:34.587
End of day two, I
have a quenched blade.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.557 line:14%
So far, so good.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:38.825 line:14%
NICK: I'm doing OK.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:39.993 line:14%
A little tired.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.094
Coffee and hate, that's
what I'm fueled by.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.029
Just kidding.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.797
Just coffee this morning.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.166
The sword looks phenomenal.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.368
Now I can really start
focusing on the fit and finish.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:53.239
So I'm going to start
working on my guard.

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:56.108
After a lot of fire
work, I get the guard

00:02:56.141 --> 00:02:58.011
bit right up to the shoulders.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.279
It looks perfect.

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:04.250
Now it's time to start
securing everything.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.286
That seam there I'll fill
with a piece of cord,

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:11.090
and then that's going to be
wrapped back to 12 inches.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:15.027
I've got to finish the handle,
but I'm comfortable that I can

00:03:15.093 --> 00:03:17.196 line:14%
get this blade done tomorrow.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.264 line:8%
JOSH: Goals for
today are getting

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:21.167
the blade cleaned up
and ground and then

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:24.404
move to working on the handle.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.706
Got the bevel ground in.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:30.343
Now I'm going to start working
on getting this handle fit up.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.878
I'm going to glue
these two pieces

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.281
together, do some sculpting.

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:36.716
I'm actually going to
make it a little bit

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:40.453
smaller than I would, because
I plan on doing a wrap.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:41.721
Have a little bit of time left.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:44.424
So start working on
the shape of the guard.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:49.495
Doing a little fit on the guard.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.700
I'm happy with the
shape, overall.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.703
Tomorrow is going to be
final assembly, glue up,

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.771
all that fun stuff.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.609
I'm just glad Will
hasn't shown up so far.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.077
I'm glad there's
no more parameters.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.145
I got plenty of them.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.347
Yeah, that'll work.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.349
 Bladesmiths,
welcome to kill test.

00:04:10.415 --> 00:04:12.752
Well, your zhanmadaos
aren't pocketknives.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:16.021
They definitely look very long,
but what kind of lethal damage

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.190
can they do?

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:18.724
To find that out, I
will take your weapons,

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:22.195
deliver some slashes and killing
blows on this boar carcass.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.062
Nick, you're up first.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:23.896
Are you ready for this?

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:24.663
 Yes, sir.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:28.635
[music playing]

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.488
 All right, Nick, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:52.691
Now, the design you have, I
was expecting a little bit more

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:53.525
of curve.

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:54.927
Because of how
straight your blade,

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:57.363
it feels more like I'm
chopping before I'm drawing.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:01.166
But as you can
see, it will kill.

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:02.367
 Thank you.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:03.436
 All right, Josh, your turn.

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:04.203
So are you ready?

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:04.970
 Let's do it.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:08.441
[music playing]

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:26.491
 All right, Josh.

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:27.860
Let's talk about
your blade here.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.529
The balance is good.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.164
And as much as I can
feel the power in there,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.468
I can wield this weapon and
develop some speed and power.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.837
And the curvature
that you have here

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:41.540
does exactly what this kind
of design is meant to do.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:45.311
Every cut was very
deep on this carcass,

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:48.047
enough to where it cut
all the way through.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:51.350
And more importantly,
it'll kill.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.184
 Thank you.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.185
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:53.251 --> 00:05:54.486
Welcome to the strength test.

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.021
And to test the strength
and overall construction

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:59.692
of your blades, I'll be chopping
into pots and this horse skull.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.560
And remember, gentlemen,
this is not about what

00:06:01.593 --> 00:06:03.028
your blades do to the targets.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.565
This is about what those targets
are going to do to your blades.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.967
Nick, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:08.734
 Yes, sir.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:12.105
[music playing]

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:28.620
 All right, Nick.

00:06:28.687 --> 00:06:30.455
So there's not
really any chipping

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:31.791
or rolling that I can feel.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.058
It's just sort of--

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.060
it's lost its fine edge.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.262
 Yes, sir.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:39.399
 Most of these weapons have a
bit more of a curve, and this--

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:42.801
it's got about a slight curve
as I could call a curve.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:43.869
 Yes, sir.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:47.106
 It's a very, very flexible
blade, but it did well.

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:47.940
So nicely done.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.308
 Thank you, sir.

00:06:49.374 --> 00:06:50.910
 All right, Josh.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:51.444
 Let's do it.

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:55.181
[music playing]

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.733
 So, Josh, very well
crafted blade, which I like.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.503
The guard, the
dimensions, the size

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.439
and the shape of the handle,
all really beautiful.

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:23.542
Unfortunately though,
we've got some rolling

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.244
on the edge of this blade.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.712
You hear that?

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:27.646
Yes.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:29.615
You put an incredibly
fine edge on this.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:33.619
And it showed in the
kill test, but not

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.788
so good for hitting pots.

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:39.325
It's a great feeling weapon, but
it did take that edge damage.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.160
 All right, bladesmiths,
now it's time to find

00:07:41.226 --> 00:07:42.528
out how sharp your blades are.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.430
This is the sharpness test,
the dual sandmen slice.

00:07:45.497 --> 00:07:46.665
Now, unlike the
strength test, this

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.433
is all about what the
edge of your blade

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.603
does to these sandmen.

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.171
Nick, you're up first.
Ready for this?

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:52.872
 Yes, sir.

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:56.142
[music playing]

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.117
[grunts]

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.489
 All right, Nick, let's
talk about your blade here.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.258
As you can see, it cut
the arms, cut the legs,

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:16.328
disemboweled the
rice off the torso.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.265
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.432
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.001
 All right, Josh,
your turn, sir.

00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:22.568
Are you ready?

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:23.335
 Let's do it.

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:26.772
[music playing]

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.710
[grunts]

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:43.923
 [bleeps] yeah.

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:50.729
 All right, Josh,
this is a cutter.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:54.567
Just a design of it really
lends itself to really draw cut.

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:58.170
The cuts are very deep and
they're very clean when

00:08:58.237 --> 00:08:59.371
you're cutting through.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:02.508
The rolling it took did not
affect its cutting ability.

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:05.544
So overall, sir, it will cut.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:07.647
Thank you.

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:10.616
 Bladesmiths, the judges'
deliberation is complete.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.451
They've made their
final decision.

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:14.954
The new "Forged in
Fire" champion is--

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:18.490
Josh.

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.259
Congratulations.

00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:21.927
Nick, your blade
didn't make the cut.

00:09:21.993 --> 00:09:24.830
Doug Marcaida is
going to tell you why.

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.099
 Nick, the zhamandao
was designed to be

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:28.801
a horse slayer or chopper.

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:31.503
The amount of flex you have
in your blade and the lack

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.272
of curvature made
it perform less

00:09:33.338 --> 00:09:35.140
than that of your competitor.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:38.643
 All right, Nick, at this
time, please leave the Forge.

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:41.046
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:44.516
 I may not be the "Forged in
Fire" champion, but by no means

00:09:44.549 --> 00:09:46.685
do I consider myself a loser.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:47.853
Congratulations, dude.

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:53.525
The sword that I
made is something

00:09:53.558 --> 00:09:55.961
that I am extremely proud of.

00:09:56.027 --> 00:09:58.396
And when it came
down to the decision,

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.799
today just wasn't my day.

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:03.035
 Congratulations, Josh.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:04.770
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:06.972
And that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.474
Come on forward and
shake our hands.

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:09.842
 I'm the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:12.378
and I don't even know
what to think right now.

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:16.048
It's something that I can
show my kids that if you put

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:18.283
your mind to something
100%, you can

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:21.153
really accomplish something.

